WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.610 --> 00:00:03.683
- Fear, to me, means
absolutely nothing anymore.

00:00:04.960 --> 00:00:07.006
Fear played such a big piece of my life,

00:00:07.006 --> 00:00:11.150
and it controlled me to not
do what was best for me,

00:00:11.150 --> 00:00:15.041
so fear to me now is
nothing but an imagination.

00:00:15.041 --> 00:00:17.708
(rhythmic beat)

00:00:22.503 --> 00:00:24.545
My name is Flip Rodriguez.
I'm a Hollywood stuntman,

00:00:24.545 --> 00:00:26.999
and on "American Ninja Warrior."

00:00:26.999 --> 00:00:29.290
In the ages of 9 to 15,

00:00:29.290 --> 00:00:30.849
I was sexually abused by my father.

00:00:30.849 --> 00:00:33.006
Like, how do I live my life after that?

00:00:33.006 --> 00:00:34.763
Like, I can't trust anybody.

00:00:35.620 --> 00:00:39.430
I got into parkour and freerunning
when I was the age of 19.

00:00:39.430 --> 00:00:40.697
Parkour and freerunning are
two different definitions

00:00:40.697 --> 00:00:41.576
that are very similar.

00:00:41.576 --> 00:00:44.240
Parkour is just straightforward: vaulting,

00:00:44.240 --> 00:00:46.486
jumping over walls, over
any obstacle in your way.

00:00:46.486 --> 00:00:49.800
Freerunning is your own
style, your own flipping,

00:00:49.800 --> 00:00:52.526
flow of it; make it nice
and pretty as possible,

00:00:52.526 --> 00:00:53.963
and you take your time.

00:00:55.068 --> 00:00:57.616
When I first got started, I
had never been upside down.

00:00:57.616 --> 00:01:00.045
So my body's like, wait,
whoa, we don't do that.

00:01:00.045 --> 00:01:01.822
And then the fear aspect kicks in.

00:01:01.822 --> 00:01:03.509
So, it's like, let's stop
and think about this.

00:01:03.509 --> 00:01:05.303
Is this really worth getting hurt?

00:01:08.629 --> 00:01:13.629
Fear is what stopped me from
trying to stop my sexual abuse.

00:01:14.376 --> 00:01:17.410
Parkour and freerunning has a
been a stepping stone for me

00:01:17.410 --> 00:01:20.292
to heal and be OK with my sexual abuse

00:01:20.292 --> 00:01:23.632
because fear is a big part
of parkour and freerunning

00:01:23.632 --> 00:01:25.358
so every day I trained,

00:01:25.358 --> 00:01:28.065
I was always encountering a new fear.

00:01:28.065 --> 00:01:30.377
I started in "American
Ninja Warrior" Season 3.

00:01:30.377 --> 00:01:31.663
- [Announcer] And look at him go!

00:01:31.663 --> 00:01:35.373
Using momentum from each
jump to get to the next one!

00:01:35.373 --> 00:01:38.350
- And then on Season 7, I
actually explained my story.

00:01:38.350 --> 00:01:39.633
I was sexually abused.

00:01:41.697 --> 00:01:44.868
After my interview came out,
I've had kids write to me.

00:01:44.868 --> 00:01:46.800
One of the parents reached out to me.

00:01:46.800 --> 00:01:48.484
Turns out that the daughter and the son

00:01:48.484 --> 00:01:51.460
were being sexually
abused by a family friend.

00:01:51.460 --> 00:01:53.790
The child just started
breaking down crying.

00:01:53.790 --> 00:01:54.623
She was like,

00:01:54.623 --> 00:01:56.481
"What Flip is talking about
is also happening to me."

00:01:56.481 --> 00:01:58.830
And they brought up charges.

00:01:58.830 --> 00:02:01.150
The gentleman got convicted of that

00:02:01.150 --> 00:02:03.360
and that right there blew my mind away

00:02:03.360 --> 00:02:06.370
because not only did I heal myself,

00:02:06.370 --> 00:02:08.580
but I also saved somebody
from further abuse

00:02:08.580 --> 00:02:10.143
and that was incredible.

00:02:12.980 --> 00:02:15.830
I like to give back to the
community with using my story.

00:02:15.830 --> 00:02:17.039
I coach parkour and freerunning.

00:02:17.039 --> 00:02:19.720
I'm not teaching them just
about parkour and freerunning.

00:02:19.720 --> 00:02:21.863
I try to teach them tools of life.

00:02:21.863 --> 00:02:23.836
You guys just saw, he
kind of fell a little bit.

00:02:23.836 --> 00:02:25.240
What do you got to say?

00:02:25.240 --> 00:02:26.441
- OK, I don't give up,

00:02:26.441 --> 00:02:29.082
and I'm gonna try this right now again

00:02:29.082 --> 00:02:32.945
because Flippy taught us to never give up.

00:02:32.945 --> 00:02:36.325
- Every single person can relate to fear.

00:02:36.325 --> 00:02:37.825
Yeah!

00:02:38.930 --> 00:02:41.690
So if I can teach these
kids, from a young age,

00:02:41.690 --> 00:02:46.193
to separate fear from
danger, that is a life tool.

00:02:47.479 --> 00:02:49.242
-Yeah, Sasha, nice!

00:02:49.242 --> 00:02:51.630
My negative piece of my life,

00:02:51.630 --> 00:02:55.016
I can now turn it around
and put a spotlight on it

00:02:55.016 --> 00:02:58.132
in the sense of this is who I am.

00:02:58.132 --> 00:02:59.964
This is what happened
to me, and look at me,

00:02:59.964 --> 00:03:01.314
I'm still shining.

00:03:01.314 --> 00:03:03.981
(rhythmic beat)

